{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class NekoAndAkiPrank {\n    private final static long MOD = 1_000_000_007;\n    private long[][] memo;\n    private int n;\n\n    public void solve() throws IOException {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        n = sc.nextInt();\n        memo = new long[2 * n][n + 1];\n        for (int i = 0; i < 2 * n; i++) {\n            for (int k = 0; k <= n; k++) {\n                memo[i][k] = -1;\n            }\n        }\n        long tWays = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i < 2 * n; i += 2) {\n            int limit = Math.min(i, 2 * n - i);\n            for (int k = 0; k <= limit; k++) {\n                tWays = (tWays + f(i, k)) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(tWays);\n    }\n\n    private long f(int i, int k) {\n        if (i == 0) {\n            return (k == 0) ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        if (memo[i][k] != -1) {\n            return memo[i][k];\n        }\n        long res;\n        if (k == 0) {\n            res = f(i - 1, 1);\n        } else if (k == n) {\n            res = f(i - 1, n - 1);\n        } else {\n            res = (f(i - 1, k - 1) + f(i - 1, k + 1)) % MOD;\n        }\n        memo[i][k] = res;\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        NekoAndAkiPrank solution = new NekoAndAkiPrank();\n        solution.solve();\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10000)\n\nclass NekoAndAkiPrank:\n    MOD = 1000000007\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.memo = None\n        self.n = 0\n\n    def solve(self):\n        data = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n        if not data:\n            return\n        self.n = int(data)\n        self.memo = [[-1] * (self.n + 1) for _ in range(2 * self.n)]\n        tWays = 0\n        for i in range(1, 2 * self.n, 2):\n            limit = min(i, 2 * self.n - i)\n            for k in range(limit + 1):\n                tWays = (tWays + self.f(i, k)) % self.MOD\n        print(tWays)\n\n    def f(self, i, k):\n        if i == 0:\n            return 1 if k == 0 else 0\n        if self.memo[i][k] != -1:\n            return self.memo[i][k]\n        if k == 0:\n            res = self.f(i - 1, 1)\n        elif k == self.n:\n            res = self.f(i - 1, self.n - 1)\n        else:\n            res = (self.f(i - 1, k - 1) + self.f(i - 1, k + 1)) % self.MOD\n        self.memo[i][k] = res\n        return res\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solution = NekoAndAkiPrank()\n    solution.solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.0265558760002023e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -3.8265450712060556e-05, -0.00034195298212580383, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.38687750697135925, -0.0019921474158763885, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0005965837044641376, -0.3132639229297638, -0.011095255613327026, -0.47408270835876465, -2.3841830625315197e-06, 0.